{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CounitSigmaOneForcesHZero","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CounitSigmaOneForcesHZero","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CounitSigmaOne.sigma_to_q_satisfies_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CounitSigmaOne.sigma_to_q_satisfies_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CounitSigmaOneForcesHZero.lean#L51-L55","doc":"**The genuine augmentation checks out**: `σ ↦ q` does satisfy the Hecke\nrelation when `h = q − q⁻¹`, i.e. `q² = (q − q⁻¹)·q + 1` — here in\ndivision-free form `q * q = (q * q - 1) + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CounitSigmaOne.no_sigma_to_one_of_h_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CounitSigmaOne.no_sigma_to_one_of_h_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CounitSigmaOneForcesHZero.lean#L44-L49","doc":"The same statement in the contrapositive form used downstream: when\n`h ≠ 0`, no unital multiplicative map can send a Hecke generator to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CounitSigmaOne.h_eq_zero_of_image_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CounitSigmaOne.h_eq_zero_of_image_one","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CounitSigmaOneForcesHZero.lean#L32-L42","doc":"**The obstruction.** If `s` satisfies the Hecke relation `s² = h·s + 1`\nand a multiplicative, unital map sends `s ↦ 1`, then `h = 0`.\n\nStated on the image side so no algebra structure is needed: `v` is the\nimage of `s`, and multiplicativity gives `v² = h·v + 1` with `v = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}